  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 353 AM CDT Tue May 12 2026\n\nLook for convective rainfall to diminish early this morning over \nsoutheast portions of the forecast area. Otherwise, the forecast \nfor the next week will feature dry weather as high pressure and \nanticylonic/subsident flow become the primary weather influences. \nThere will be some concern for fog early Wednesday morning given \nthe clearing skies, light surface wind, and a humid boundary \nlayer, and so will go ahead and message a limited threat for \ndense fog in the graphics. Fog will need to be monitored for each \nmorning in this return flow pattern. A weak/dry cold front \ncrossing the forecast area Wednesday night will be inconsequential\nin terms of weather impacts in the forecast area. /EC/",
